O|               The most difficult subjects can be explained to the most slow-       
O|               witted man if he has not formed any idea of them already; but        
O|               the simplest thing cannot be made clear to the most                  
O|               intelligent man if he is firmly persuaded that he knows              
O|               already, without a shadow of doubt, what is laid before him.         
O|
