S|       1       OPEN ON: INT. SOLOMON BROTHERS - 1979 - DAY              1           
O|
N|               A bunch of FAT BOND TRADERS eat deli sandwiches and smoke            
N|               cigarettes on the Solomon Brothers Bond Trading floor. It’s          
N|               not exactly Michael Douglas in Wall Street.                          
O|
N|               The voice that walks us through this is smart, too the point         
N,M|               and slick. We’ll meet him later.                                     
O|
C,E|                                   MODERN TRADER (V.O.)                             
U|                         In the late seventies banking was                          
U|                         not a job you went into to make                            
U|                         large sums of money. It was a good                         
U|                         stable profession like selling                             
U|                         insurance or accounting. And if                            
U|                         banking was boring then the bond                           
U|                         department at a bank was downright                         
U|                         comatose. We all know about bonds,                         
U|                         give em to your nephew when he                             
U|                         turns 16 and then we he’s thirty he                        
U|                         makes a hundred dollars. Yawn.                             
U|                         Bonds were for losers. That is,                            
U|                         until Lewis Ranieri came on the                            
U|                         scene at Solomon Brothers...                               
N,M|               MUSIC: Some great 70’s ballad like KISS YOU ALL OVER by EXILE        
N,G,I|               We see an even schlubbier version of the other Bond Traders          
N,I|               emerge. His suit is rumpled, he has a mustard stain on his           
N,I|               shirt from a soft pretzel he’s eating and he is easily               
N,I|               seventy pounds over weight. This is LEWIS RENIERI. And though        
N|               his world is obscure, he is the shit.                                
O|
N,G|               Our NARRATOR the MODERN TRADER passes through the scene for a        
N|               second, dressed in modern clothes...                                 
O|
N|               Lewis greets his Bond Department with obscenities barked             
N|               through his patchy beard and glasses.                                
C,E|                                   MODERN TRADER (V.O.)                             
U|                         You see Lewis didn’t know it yet,                          
U|                         but he had already changed banking                         
U|                         forever. He had just one simple                            
U|                         idea...                                                    
O|
