U|                         Basically Lewis Ranieri’s Mortgage                         
U|                         bonds were amazingly profitable for                        
U|                         the big banks. They made billions                          
U|                         and billions off of their 2% fee on                        
U|                         each of these bonds they sold. But                         
U|                         then they started running out of                           
U|                         mortgages to put in them. After                            
U|                         all, there’s only so many homes and                        
U|                         so many people with good enough                            
U|                         jobs to buy them. So the banks                             
U|                         starting doing something different.                        
U|                         Instead of creating mortgage bonds                         
U|                         that were guaranteed by the US                             
U|                         government, they started creating                          
U|                         their own private mortgage bonds.                          
U|                         No government, no pesky standards                          
U|                         like good credit or minimum income.                        
U|                         And then the big banks were able to                        
U|                         fill the bonds with riskier and                            
U|                         riskier mortgages and keep the                             
U|                         profit machine churning. By the                            
U|                         way, the risky mortgages are called                        
U|                         “subprime.” Anytime you hear                               
U|                         subprime, think shit.                                      
O|                                   (MORE)                                           
O|
O|
O|                           BUFF REVISED, MAY 11, 2015              13A.             
O|
C,E|                                   SCARLETT JOHANSSON (CONT'D)                      
U|                         Michael Burry found out these                              
U|                         mortgage bonds that we supposedly                          
U|                         65% AAA were actually mostly full                          
U|                         of shit, so now he’s going to                              
U|                         “short” the bonds, which means to                          
U|                         “bet against.” Got it? Good.                               
